===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|σπέρμα||sperm|lang=grc}} + {{term|ζῷον||living thing|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌspɜːmətə(ʊ)ˈzəʊɒn/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|spermatozoa}}

# {{context|cytology|lang=en}} A reproductive cell or [[gamete]] of a male, carried in [[semen]], that fertilizes an [[ovum]] to produce a [[zygote]].

====Synonyms====
